---
description: Cross-cutting rules for strata-forge — always-on. Defers to `CLAUDE.md` for the full source of truth.
alwaysApply: true
---

strata-forge is a typed, async-first, vendor-neutral toolkit for AI/LLM work. The distribution is
`strata-forge`; the import package is `strata_forge`. **Read [`CLAUDE.md`](mdc:CLAUDE.md) before
suggesting non-trivial changes.** Module-specific rules live in `src/strata_forge/<module>/CLAUDE.md`;
[`docs/agent-guide.md`](mdc:docs/agent-guide.md) is the long-form playbook for orientation, task
recipes, and the verification loop.

Always-on rules:

- Every public function that performs I/O is `async`. Pure helpers (`get_settings`, `render`,
  `content_hash`, registry lookups, `Chunker.chunk`) stay synchronous. Sync wrappers live **only** in
  `strata_forge.sync`, which covers four `LLMClient` methods; the CLI bridges through its own
  `run_async` helper in `cli/helpers.py`. `SFTRunner.train` / `PreferenceRunner.train` are the one
  documented sync exception, because TRL's loop is blocking.
- pyright strict on `src/strata_forge`. No `Any` without a `# pyright: ignore[reportXxx] — reason` on
  the same line. Ruff line length 100; `ruff format` is authoritative.
- Errors are exception-based. Runtime failures a caller might catch subclass
  `strata_forge.core.errors.ForgeError`; a bad argument at the call boundary stays `ValueError` /
  `TypeError`. Never `except:`, never swallow — the one sanctioned swallow is `strata_forge.tracing`,
  which must never break a caller's hot path.
- Heavy deps (`torch`, `transformers`, `trl`, `peft`, `datasets`, `skypilot`, `asyncssh`,
  `qdrant-client`, `cohere`, `sentence-transformers`, `fsspec` + cloud filesystems,
  `huggingface_hub`, `langfuse`, `redis`, `pillow`, `nltk`, `boto3`) are imported **inside the
  function that uses them**, never at module load. Each gates behind an extra in `pyproject.toml`,
  and the enclosing function raises `ImportError` naming the real distribution:
  `pip install 'strata-forge[<extra>]'`. `ai-forge` is a different project and must never appear in a
  hint, a doc, or an example.
- Model-provider SDKs (`anthropic`, `openai`, `boto3`, Google's clients) are imported **only inside
  `src/strata_forge/llm/providers/`** — plus one deliberate exception, `llm/errors.py`, which imports
  `openai` to name the exception classes LiteLLM re-raises. Everything else goes through `LLMClient`
  or the `provider_extras={...}` passthrough.
- Configuration flows through `strata_forge.config.get_settings()`. Do not read `os.environ`
  elsewhere.
- No emojis anywhere in the repository — source, docs, headings, tables, or commit messages. The
  badges at the top of the root `README.md` are the only exception.
- Every symbol written into a doc, example, or error message must exist. Verify against
  `src/strata_forge` before writing an import or a call.
- Commits MUST follow Conventional Commits: `<type>(<optional-scope>): <imperative summary>`. Allowed
  types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.
  Scope is the module name (`feat(llm):`, `docs(rag):`) when the change is local to one module; omit
  it for cross-cutting work. Commit messages, branch names, and PR titles use **time-stable
  language** — never phase numbers, step numbers, or plan-file slugs. See `CLAUDE.md` §8.
- Topic branch off `dev`, PR into `dev`. `main` only ever receives `dev`, through a promotion PR.
  Never `--no-verify`, never force-push a shared branch.
- **Self-maintenance protocol** (CLAUDE.md §7): when you spot a stale `CLAUDE.md` / MDC rule / ADR /
  module README, fix it in the same PR. Merged code wins over a stale rule; the rule file wins over
  in-flight code. ADRs are immutable — supersede, never edit. Never silently ignore a stale rule.
